2.0.1:
[Change] conf.bfd reorganized into 5 clearly labeled sections: Detection
         Thresholds, Ban Actions, Email Alerts, Log Paths, Logging & Advanced;
         "You should not need to edit" separator eliminated — all remaining
         variables are user-configurable
[New] internals.conf: internal/derived variables (RULES_PATH, TLOG_PATH,
      EMAIL_TEMPLATE, IGNORE_HOST_FILES, LOCK_FILE, TIME_ZONE) split from
      conf.bfd into separate file; users never need to edit these
[Change] LOG_SOURCE promoted from below separator to Log Paths section;
         comment updated to clarify journal mode now behaves same as auto
[Change] TIME_UNIX dead variable removed (redundant with UTIME in bfd);
         INSTALL_PATH removed from conf.bfd (hardcoded in bfd before conf.bfd
         is sourced, changing it in conf.bfd alone had no effect)
[Change] files/bfd sources internals.conf after conf.bfd with same safety
         checks (root ownership, not world-writable); fallback defaults for
         all internals.conf variables ensure backward compat with pre-split
         installs
[Change] importconf: merge_conf() function extracted; dual-merge handles
         both conf.bfd and internals.conf; for pre-split upgrades, old
         conf.bfd variables migrate to new internals.conf; journal cursor
         and timestamp state preserved during upgrades
[New] 2 importconf tests: pre-split variable migration to internals.conf,
      post-split upgrade merging both old files; full suite now 451 tests
[Fix] tlog_journal_filter: rh_ipop3d case key mismatched TLOG_TF="rh_ipop3"
      set by the rh_ipop3d rule file; journal fallback silently failed for
      POP3 rules; corrected to rh_ipop3
[Fix] tlog_read/tlog journal dispatch: LOG_SOURCE=journal bypassed existing
      log files, hijacking rules like vsftpd2 whose TLOG_TF matched journal
      mappings but whose LP pointed to application-specific logs; dispatch
      now requires file to be missing regardless of LOG_SOURCE setting
[Fix] cron.daily: .cursor and .jts files accumulated in tmp/ without cleanup;
      added rm -f for *.cursor and *.jts during daily rotation
[New] tlog_journal_filter test for rh_ipop3 → ipop3d mapping
[Change] tlog_read forced-journal test updated to expect file mode when file
         exists (matches simplified dispatch logic); full suite now 449 tests
[New] systemd journal reader with transparent fallback: when a rule's flat
      log file is missing but journalctl is available, BFD reads from the
      systemd journal instead; 15 of 30 rules are journal-capable (sshd,
      dropbear, dovecot, postfix, courier, sendmail, vpopmail, cyrus,
      pure-ftpd, proftpd, vsftpd, webmin, wordpress, rh_imapd, rh_ipop3d)
[New] LOG_SOURCE config variable: auto (default, journal fallback), file
      (flat files only, for CentOS 6), or journal (prefer journal for
      syslog-based rules)
[New] tlog_journal_filter() maps TLOG_TF names to SYSLOG_IDENTIFIER
      journalctl filters via case statement with 15 service mappings
[New] tlog_journal_read() reads new journal entries with cursor-based
      tracking (primary) and Unix timestamp fallback; first run saves
      cursor and outputs nothing (matches tlog first-run behavior);
      invalid cursors (journal vacuumed) fall back to timestamp; all
      journalctl calls wrapped with timeout 30
[Change] tlog_read() adds journal dispatch: when LOG_SOURCE=journal or
         file is missing in auto mode, delegates to tlog_journal_read()
         for journal-capable rules before falling back to file error
[Change] validate_rule() relaxes LP file check: allows rules where LP is
         missing if journalctl is available and TLOG_TF has a journal
         mapping (unless LOG_SOURCE=file)
[Change] validate_config() validates LOG_SOURCE (must be auto, file, or
         journal)
[Change] health_check() adds journalctl availability status, LOG_SOURCE
         setting display, and journal-aware rule scan that shows
         "active via journal" for rules using journal fallback
[Change] files/tlog adds journal dispatch: sources bfd.lib.sh lazily
         only in the journal path; no performance impact on file-based
         systems
[Change] files/bfd exports LOG_SOURCE in pre() for tlog subprocess access
[New] tests/test_tlog_journal.bats with 27 tests: tlog_journal_filter
      mappings (7), tlog_journal_read cursor/timestamp/fallback (8),
      tlog_read dispatch logic (6), validate_rule journal awareness (4),
      validate_config LOG_SOURCE validation (2); mocked journalctl
[Fix] test_validate_rule.bats: LP-missing test now sets LOG_SOURCE=file
      to prevent journal fallback on systems with journalctl
[Note] zero modifications to any of the 30 rule files; journal output
       format (--output=short) is syslog-compatible with existing
       extract_hosts() patterns; full suite now 448 tests
[Change] importconf rewritten: grep/awk-based config merge replaces
         source+heredoc approach; user values (including template variables
         like $ATTACK_HOST) preserved as raw text without shell expansion;
         new variables get defaults, removed variables dropped; .ca.def and
         .conf.bfd dual-template files eliminated — files/conf.bfd is now
         the single source of truth for both fresh installs and upgrades
[Change] importconf state file copies made explicit: only bans.active,
         bans.history*, events.dat, stats/*, and ignore.hosts are preserved;
         replaces cp tmp/* + selective rm approach
[Change] importconf version extraction uses awk on header comment instead
         of fragile tac | tail -n 3 | grep BFD | awk pipeline
[New] tests/test_importconf.bats with 8 tests: fresh install exit, simple
      value preservation, template variable preservation ($ATTACK_HOST),
      new variable defaults, removed variable dropping, comment/structure
      preservation, version extraction, state file copying
[Fix] IPv6 false-match bug: grep -Fw treats colons as word boundaries, causing
      prefix false positives (2001:db8::1 matches 2001:db8::10). Replaced with
      awk field-exact matching ($3 == ip) for bans.active lookups and grep -Fx
      for single-IP-per-line files (ban.list, ignore.hosts). Affected functions:
      state_bans_active_append, state_bans_active_remove, state_bans_active_check,
      _apool_ban_status, state_ban_check, state_ban_append, state_track_count,
      filter_host, manual_unban
[Fix] Local address detection: grep -Ew 'inet6? ' failed to match IPv4 inet
      lines (word boundary after trailing space meets digit), causing local IPv4
      addresses to be missing from LO_HOSTS; changed to grep -E without -w
[Fix] Attack pool search (bfd -a STRING) used grep -E treating dots and other
      characters as regex wildcards; changed to grep -F for literal matching
[Fix] Documentation: nftables missing UNBAN_COMMAND example, health check
      [SKIP] indicator undocumented, TLOG_TF described as log path instead of
      tracking identifier, weekly attack pool report not mentioned
[New] 14 regression tests: IPv6 exact-match for bans.active (append, remove,
      check, dedup), ban.list, ignore.hosts, attack pool ban status, recidivism,
      full ban lifecycle flow, literal search matching, lo_hosts pipeline IPv4/IPv6
      capture; suite now 413 tests
[New] Per-run statistics in check(): rules_count, events_count, bans_count,
      elapsed time (seconds); logged via eout at end of each run
[New] health_check() non-destructive diagnostic: validates config, log paths,
      BAN_COMMAND binaries, rule activation (active vs inactive with REQ
      checks), tlog, state directories, lock files, active ban count;
      formatted PASS/WARN/FAIL/SKIP output with summary
[New] -c|--check CLI flag for health check and diagnostics
[New] _apool_ban_status() returns ban status per IP: BANNED(perm) for
      permanent, BANNED(Xm) for temp with remaining minutes, prev:N for
      historical ban count from bans.history
[New] STATUS column added to _apool_report() attack summary output
[New] _apool_service_summary() per-service breakdown: event counts and
      unique IP counts per service, sorted by event count descending
[Change] apool_list() shows per-service breakdown after daily report
[Change] Wholesale README rewrite modeled on APF documentation structure:
         header with copyright/license, table of contents, quick start guide,
         subsectioned configuration (detection, banning, escalation, IPv6,
         alerts, log paths), firewall integration with paired ban/unban
         examples, general usage with dry run/health check/attack pool
         subsections, rule engine with catalog table and customization guide,
         ignore lists, ban management lifecycle, IPv6 support, troubleshooting
         table, corrected support URLs
[New] README.md: full Markdown version with badges, anchor-linked table of
      contents, tables for config/rules/troubleshooting, fenced code blocks
      for all command examples
[New] tests/test_health_check.bats with 15 tests for health check mode
[New] tests/test_apool.bats with 10 tests for enhanced attack summary
[New] 5 run statistics tests in test_check_pipeline.bats (62 total);
      full suite now 399 tests
[New] validate_ip6() for IPv6 address validation: full 8-group, ::
      compression, zone ID stripping (%eth0), mixed case; rejects
      malformed addresses, triple colon, multiple ::, injection attempts
[New] validate_ip_any() dual-stack validator: tries IPv4 first, falls back
      to IPv6; single entry point for all IP validation
[New] extract_hosts() dual IPv4/IPv6 extraction: IPv6 regex alongside IPv4
      with boundary-aware [^0-9a-fA-F:] prefix; validate_ip_any() in output
      pipeline accepts both address families
[New] BAN_COMMAND_V6 config variable for IPv6-specific ban commands with
      ip6tables, nft, ip route examples; empty = use BAN_COMMAND for both
[New] UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 config variable for IPv6-specific unban commands
[Change] HOSTS_PARSED pipeline simplified: removed tr ':' ' ' | awk that
         destroyed IPv6 addresses; sort -n changed to sort
[Change] check() uses validate_ip_any() instead of validate_ip() to accept
         both IPv4 and IPv6 through the detection pipeline
[Fix] count_failures() uses grep -cxF (exact line match) instead of
      grep -cFw to prevent IPv6 false positives from colon word boundaries
[Change] execute_ban()/execute_unban() select V6 command template for IPv6
         hosts when BAN_COMMAND_V6/UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 configured; fall back to
         standard commands when V6 templates empty
[Change] process_unbans() passes UNBAN_COMMAND_V6_TEMPLATE for IPv6 hosts
[Change] manual_ban()/manual_unban() accept IPv6 addresses and pass V6
         templates; validate_ip_any() replaces validate_ip()
[Change] LO_HOSTS uses grep -E 'inet6? ' to capture both IPv4 and IPv6
         local addresses, preventing self-banning
[New] tests/test_validate_ip6.bats: 33 tests for IPv6 validation and
      validate_ip_any() dual-stack behavior
[New] 8 IPv6 extraction tests in test_extract_hosts.bats (23 total)
[New] 5 IPv6 regex sample lines and tests in regex_samples.txt/bats (53 total)
[New] 13 IPv6 pipeline tests in test_check_pipeline.bats (57 total): counting,
      false-positive prevention, V6 command selection, local address detection,
      manual ban/unban IPv6; full suite now 369 tests
[New] extract_hosts() declarative rule engine with fail2ban-compatible <HOST>
      placeholder patterns; boundary-aware sed extraction prevents greedy .*
      from consuming leading IP digits
[New] IGNOREREGEX support for per-rule line exclusion (fail2ban-compatible)
[New] tests/regex_samples.txt: CSF-inspired sample log lines for all 30 rules
[New] tests/test_regex_samples.bats: 48 automated pattern validation tests
[New] tests/test_extract_hosts.bats: 15 unit tests for extract_hosts()
[New] 10 new service rules from fail2ban/CSF patterns: apache-auth,
      nginx-http-auth, mysqld-auth, wordpress, webmin, directadmin,
      cyrus-imap, roundcube, plesk, dropbear (30 rules total)
[Change] all 20 existing rules converted from ad-hoc grep/sed/awk pipelines
         to extract_hosts() with FAILREGEX patterns
[New] $PORTS substitution in BAN_COMMAND/UNBAN_COMMAND templates for
      port-specific firewall rules (rule files define PORTS per service)
[New] port-aware iptables/nftables ban command examples in conf.bfd
[Change] execute_ban accepts 5th parameter (ports); sets PORTS and MOD globals
         for template expansion
[Change] execute_unban accepts 4th parameter (ports); sets PORTS global for
         template expansion
[Change] process_unbans passes stored PORTS from bans.active to unban commands
[Change] manual_unban reads PORTS from ban state for unban command expansion
[Change] manual_ban accepts optional ports parameter (default "all")
[New] 8 tests for PORTS enforcement in test_check_pipeline.bats (44 total);
      full suite now 247 tests
[Fix] removed dead SKIP variable and vestigial if-wrapper in check(); dedup
      now handled by state_bans_active_check
[Fix] removed unreachable tlog library delegation branch (tlog_read never
      available in subprocess context)
[Fix] list_bans header/data piped through single format_table call for
      aligned column widths
[Fix] unknown CLI flags now print error and exit non-zero instead of
      silently showing help
[Fix] cron.daily purges rotated bans.history files older than 30 days
[Fix] removed dead else branch in manual_ban (mod always non-empty via
      default)
[Fix] importconf targeted cleanup preserves ban lifecycle state (bans.active,
      bans.history, events.dat) during upgrades instead of rm -f tmp/*
[Fix] state_init() called in pre() so state files are created with 600
      permissions before first use, preventing world-readable state
[Fix] check() verifies execute_ban return code; failed bans no longer
      recorded in bans.active/bans.history (phantom ban prevention)
[New] test for failed ban command skipping lifecycle recording
      (test_check_pipeline.bats, 36 total); full suite now 239 tests
[New] BAN_DURATION config variable (default 300s) for temporary bans with
      auto-expiry; 0 = permanent ban (legacy behavior)
[New] BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER config variable (default 5) for recidivism
      escalation: repeat temp-bans become permanent
[New] BAN_PERMANENT_WINDOW config variable (default 86400s/24h) for
      counting repeat offenses toward permanent ban threshold
[New] UNBAN_COMMAND config variable with APF, iptables, firewalld,
      nftables, and ip route examples
[New] ban state tracking via bans.active (active bans with expiry) and
      bans.history (append-only ban event log) in tmp/
[New] state_bans_active_append/remove/check/list/expired functions for
      managing active ban state with duplicate prevention
[New] state_bans_history_append and state_bans_count_recent for ban
      event logging and recidivism counting
[New] execute_unban() mirrors execute_ban for removing bans
[New] process_unbans() auto-expires temporary bans each cron cycle,
      executing UNBAN_COMMAND and recording unban events
[New] check_recidivism() escalates repeat offenders to permanent bans
      when BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER threshold met within window
[New] -l|--list CLI flag displays active bans with formatted table
[New] -u|--unban CLI flag manually unbans an IP address
[New] -b|--ban CLI flag manually bans an IP address permanently
[New] list_bans, manual_unban, manual_ban functions in bfd.lib.sh
[Change] run() calls process_unbans before check() to clear expired bans
[Change] check() skips hosts with active bans; records bans in lifecycle
         state with recidivism-aware expiry calculation
[Change] validate_config() validates BAN_DURATION, BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER,
         BAN_PERMANENT_WINDOW; warns if BAN_DURATION>0 with no UNBAN_COMMAND
[Fix] cron.daily replaced rm -f tmp/* with targeted cleanup preserving
      bans.active and events.dat; rotates bans.history daily
[Change] state_init() creates bans.active and bans.history alongside
         existing state files
[New] tests/test_ban_lifecycle.bats with 26 tests for ban state functions
[New] 14 tests for ban lifecycle integration and CLI in
      test_check_pipeline.bats
[New] 10 tests for ban config validation in test_config_validation.bats
      (34 total)
[Change] per-service TRIG thresholds enabled in all 20 rule files: sshd=5,
         dovecot=10, postfix=10, vsftpd/vsftpd2=10, proftpd=10, pure-ftpd=10,
         exim_authfail=10, exim_nxuser=15, modsec=10, asterisk_badauth=5,
         asterisk_iax=5, asterisk_nopeer=5, openvpnas=5, cpanel=5, courier=10,
         vpopmail=10, rh_imapd=10, rh_ipop3d=10, sendmail=10
[Change] check() uses count_failures() with time-windowed counting instead
         of count_attacks(); events pruned once per run before iterating rules
[New] TRIG_GLOBAL cross-service check in check(): when per-rule threshold
      not met but aggregate failures across all services exceed TRIG_GLOBAL
[Change] test_check_pipeline.bats updated with count_failures tests, TRIG_GLOBAL
         tests, and windowed pipeline integration tests (21 total)
[New] state_events_append() appends timestamped failure events to events.dat
[New] state_events_count() counts events for a host within a time window,
      with optional per-service filtering using mawk-compatible awk
[New] state_events_prune() removes expired events with safety cap (default 5000)
[New] count_failures() replaces count_attacks() with time-windowed counting;
      appends timestamped events and returns per-service windowed count
[Change] state_init() now creates events.dat alongside track.attack and ban.list
[New] tests/test_events.bats with 24 tests covering state_events_append,
      state_events_count, state_events_prune, count_failures, and state_init
[New] TRIG_WINDOW config variable (default 300s) for time-windowed failure
      counting; only failures within this window count toward threshold
[New] TRIG_GLOBAL config variable (default 0/disabled) for cross-service
      aggregate threshold regardless of per-rule TRIG values
[Change] validate_config() validates TRIG_WINDOW (positive integer) and
         TRIG_GLOBAL (non-negative integer)
[New] 8 tests for TRIG_WINDOW and TRIG_GLOBAL validation in
      test_config_validation.bats (24 total)
[New] tests/test_filter_host.bats with 12 tests for ignore list and local
      address filtering
[New] tests/test_check_pipeline.bats with 15 integration tests for
      count_attacks, execute_ban, and end-to-end pipeline
[New] filter_host() in bfd.lib.sh checks ignore lists and local addresses;
      returns 0 (process), 1 (ignored), or 2 (local address)
[New] count_attacks() in bfd.lib.sh counts host occurrences and accumulates
      track.attack history using state_track_* functions
[New] execute_ban() in bfd.lib.sh executes or dry-run logs ban commands
[Change] check() in bfd decomposed from 99 to 40 lines; delegates to
         filter_host, count_attacks, execute_ban, validate_rule,
         state_ban_append, state_pool_append
[New] tlog_read() in bfd.lib.sh implements tlog byte-offset tracking as a
      library function, avoiding subprocess overhead per rule
[Change] files/tlog delegates to tlog_read() when bfd.lib.sh is loaded,
         with standalone fallback for backward compatibility
[New] 7 additional tlog_read tests in tests/test_tlog.bats (14 total)
[New] validate_rule() in bfd.lib.sh verifies LP, TLOG_TF, ARG_VAL after
      rule sourcing; returns 1 with diagnostic on skip
[New] tests/test_validate_rule.bats with 9 tests for rule validation
[New] state file I/O functions in bfd.lib.sh: state_init, state_track_append,
      state_track_count, state_track_trim, state_ban_check, state_ban_append,
      state_pool_append
[New] tests/test_state_io.bats with 20 tests for state file I/O functions
[Change] test suite migrated from custom assert framework to BATS 1.11.0
         with bats-support 0.3.0 and bats-assert 2.1.0
[New] 9 Dockerfiles for multi-OS test execution (Debian 12, CentOS 6/7,
      Rocky 8/9/10, Ubuntu 12.04/20.04/24.04)
[New] tests/run-tests.sh Docker-based test runner with --os flag
[New] tests/Makefile with sequential and parallel targets for all OS tiers
[New] tests/helpers/bfd-common.bash shared BATS helper sourcing bfd.lib.sh
[Change] .github/workflows/ci.yml rebuilt with 8-OS Docker matrix, Buildx
         caching, separate lint and test jobs
[Change] all 7 test files converted from .sh with custom asserts to .bats
         format (87 tests)
[New] run() function in bfd consolidates pre/get_state/check dispatch
[New] usage() function extracted from inline case statement help text
[Change] case statement simplified: -s/-q/-d branches call run() instead of
         duplicating pre; get_state; check
[New] validate_ip() function for strict octet 0-255 IP validation using BASH_REMATCH
[New] sanitize_mod() function restricts rule names to alphanumeric, underscore, hyphen
[New] safe_source() validates root ownership and non-world-writable before sourcing files
[New] cleanup trap on EXIT/INT/TERM releases lock files and flock FD
[Fix] eliminated command injection in BAN_COMMAND execution; removed temp file
      approach and config re-sourcing from hot loop
[Fix] secured temp files with mktemp replacing predictable PID-based names
[Fix] atomic locking with flock replacing TOCTOU check-then-act race condition
[Fix] tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat read-only approach
[Fix] alert.bfd variable quoting and grep -Fw for literal IP matching
[Change] backtick command substitution replaced with $() in bfd and alert.bfd
[Change] deprecated $[expr] arithmetic replaced with $((expr)) in get_state
[New] detect_log_paths() auto-detects AUTH, KERNEL, MAIL log paths for
      cross-distro compatibility (RHEL/Debian/Ubuntu)
[New] MAIL_LOG_PATH config variable for mail log path detection
[New] format_table() wrapper with column fallback to tr for minimal systems
[New] get_file_size() wrapper in tlog with stat fallback to wc -c
[Change] hardcoded /sbin/ip replaced with command -v discovery and hostname -I
         fallback
[Change] egrep replaced with grep -E across all rule files
[Change] hardcoded mail log paths replaced with $MAIL_LOG_PATH in 5 rules
         (dovecot, sendmail, courier, vpopmail, postfix)
[Change] sendmail rule REQ changed from /etc/init.d/sendmail to /usr/sbin/sendmail
[Change] added firewall examples in conf.bfd (iptables, firewalld, nftables,
         ip route) with BAN_COMMAND binary existence warning
[Fix] deprecated $[expr] arithmetic replaced with $((expr)) in check()
[Fix] BAN_COMMAND template now extracted raw from conf.bfd to prevent
      premature $ATTACK_HOST/$MOD expansion at source time
[Change] systematic variable quoting across bfd, tlog, conf.bfd,
         importconf, install.sh, uninstall.sh, cron.daily
[Change] backtick command substitution replaced with $() across all
         remaining files (tlog, conf.bfd, importconf, cron.daily,
         install.sh, and 18 rule files)
[Change] for-cat and for-ls antipatterns replaced with while-read loops
         and process substitution in bfd
[New] validate_config() function validates TRIG, EMAIL_ALERTS,
      LOCK_FILE_TIMEOUT, BAN_COMMAND, INSTALL_PATH at startup
[New] meaningful exit codes (EXIT_OK, EXIT_CONFIG_ERROR, EXIT_LOCK_ERROR,
      EXIT_PREREQ_ERROR) replace bare exit 1 throughout bfd
[Change] eout() refactored with local variables and single timestamp
[Change] apool_list() refactored with _apool_report() helper eliminating
         tripled code
[Fix] uninitialized LAST_HOST, LAST, SKIP_ALERT variables now initialized
[Fix] -a without argument no longer causes unbound variable error
[Fix] install.sh: added root check, set -eu, explicit mkdir tmp/,
      quoting, backtick replacement
[Change] tlog expr arithmetic replaced with $(()) throughout
[Change] copyright years updated to 2026 across all modified files
[Change] _apool_report() rewritten with single-pass awk replacing
         4 greps per IP (100 greps per report reduced to 1 awk pass)
[Change] ARG_VAL tr/awk/sort pipeline processed once per rule instead
         of N+1 times (once per unique host + once for iteration)
[New] bfd.lib.sh function library extracted for testability
      (validate_ip, sanitize_mod, eout, safe_source, validate_config,
      detect_log_paths, format_table)
[New] test suite with 58 tests (test_validate_ip, test_detect_log_paths,
      test_config_validation) using simple assert framework
[New] -d|--dryrun flag runs detection without executing ban commands
[New] -v|--version and -h|--help CLI flags
[New] systemd bfd.service and bfd.timer for optional systemd scheduling
[Change] install.sh conditionally installs systemd timer when systemd
         is available; cron remains primary scheduler
[Change] uninstall.sh cleans up systemd timer and cron.daily
[New] .shellcheckrc and full shellcheck compliance across all scripts
[New] .github/workflows/ci.yml for shellcheck and test automation
[Change] README updated with supported distro matrix, firewall examples,
         dry-run usage, rule customization, and troubleshooting
[Fix] tlog log rotation bug: duplicate output when log rotates; remainder
      from rotated file plus entire current file caused repeated lines
[Fix] tlog line 57 misplaced redirection on TSIZE assignment
[Fix] -q flag no longer spawns redundant subprocess; uses exec
      redirection to suppress output in-process
[Change] .ca.def and .conf.bfd importconf templates updated to 2.0.1
         with new copyrights, $() syntax, MAIL_LOG_PATH, firewall
         examples, EMAIL_LOGLINES, LOCK_FILE_TIMEOUT=300
[Fix] alert.bfd: removed dead EB variable (set but never read)
[New] EMAIL_LOGLINES config variable exposed in conf.bfd (default 50)
[Fix] modsec rule: FILE variable renamed to LP for alert compatibility;
      added Debian /var/log/apache2/error.log path detection;
      deduplicated ARG_VAL pipeline across if/elif branches
[Fix] vsftpd rule: removed redundant duplicate sed/grep pipeline pass
[Change] removed unused TMP variable from sshd, asterisk_badauth,
         asterisk_iax, asterisk_nopeer rules
[Change] quoted $TLOG_PATH, $LP, $TLOG_TF in ARG_VAL pipelines across
         all 20 rule files
[New] PORTS defined for asterisk_badauth (5060,5061), asterisk_iax
      (4569), asterisk_nopeer (5060,5061)
[New] test suite expanded from 58 to 99 tests: added test_eout (11),
      test_safe_source (11), test_format_table (10), test_tlog (9)
[Change] tlog BASERUN now overridable via environment for testability
[Change] normalized rule file indentation to tabs and removed trailing
         whitespace across all 20 rule files
[Change] version renamed from 1.6-1 to 2.0.1 across all files
[Change] project domain normalized to rfxn.com (replaced r-fx.org)
